Field definitions:
- complexity: how conceptually hard the task is to reason about, independent of how long it takes.
- subsystems_touched: rough count of distinct code areas or services the description references, 0 to 10.
- needs_live_verification: true only if closing this task requires checking a running system — a server, a deployed service, live data — rather than just passing tests.
- risk_class: "safety_publish_payments" if the task touches a safety gate, publishing, or payments; "data" if it touches migrations, schemas, or stored data; otherwise "none".
- duration_class: rough wall-clock size of the work — short, medium, or long.
- work_kind: the dominant kind of work — build (new code), review (checking existing work), diagnose (root-causing a defect), or docs (documentation only).

